invariant: INV-50
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: end_block leaves b ^ c as the last round wrote it, a ^ b of the
  working variables before the state was added to them, so the first
  round of the next block in the same call computes Maj from a stale
  value. A call over one block is right, and so is every digest of a
  message that never hands the function two blocks at once: HMAC's one
  block a call, and FIPS 180-4's short vectors. A record's transcript and
  a certificate are not. bin/sha2_equiv_test hands it two and more blocks
  in one update, and those cases differ from the reference, whose
  function takes one block a call.

--- old
    state[7] = v->h;
    v->b_xor_c = v->b ^ v->c;
--- new
    state[7] = v->h;
